;; Ichigo's general arms (PLAN4 §3, batch B3; assembled, no search). One style function, ichigo-ki-r2b2a1-style, so a switch keeps its state.
;; The common base = the KI table's 2026-11-15 arm 0 (x-ki-i-r1-b0a2) without its exchange keys (they come from the pairing's :with unit,
;; x-units/) and without its mode mix. Arm 0 `all` names no :iks-mix-* key: it plays the style's own mix for the tier (HARD: generic 0.04,
;; space 0.26, whiff 0.26, ptr3 0.28, kessa 0.16; EASY generic only). Each job arm names all five mix keys: its mode at 1, the rest at 0
;; (KNOBS.md §6.3: a named key keeps the tier's other weights, so naming one alone would not be one job). No arm names an exchange key.
;; One plist per arm, arm 0 first; proof.py reads them by :id.
(:id :a4-i-all :fn ichigo-ki-r2b2a1-style :apply (:ichigo) :base (:ikw-roll-x 0.7 :ikw-roll-y 0.7 :range 0.7 :ns 0.35 :hoho 0.5 :cont 1.3 :awaken 3.0 :p 1.0 :b-walk-in 0.06 :b-j1 0.05 :b-step-in 0.03 :b-wait -0.05 :b-walk-out -0.08 :b-step-out -0.05 :iks-wait-max 40 :iks-gap-p 1.0 :iks-gap-fs 150 :iks-ns-wait 24 :iks-getsuga-min 6.5 :iks-meaty-p 0.0) :rules ((((:ost :down)) (:b-walk-in 0.14 :b-j1 0.12 :b-wait -0.12)) (((:dj :in)) (:b-j1 0.12 :b-step-out -0.1)) (((:dj :afar)) (:b-walk-in 0.12 :b-step-in 0.08)) (((:ost :active) (:dj :in)) (:b-hoho -0.05))))
